# THE FOUR-TOWN RUN CONTINUED FROM 175,000 WITH THE FAULT CHARGE AT 10 AND THE RESUME WARM-UP
# (user 2026-11-15: "go ahead").
# = slurm/cluster_frl_c0actor_privcritic_4towns_ar2_lc01_miss_fault10_resume_par.env (job 466557) with ONLY:
#   FRL_RESUME_FREEZE=15000: after the resume the critic alone is updated until the fresh replay holds
#   15,000 own rows; the actor and the temperature are held until then (torch_rl.frl.carla resume_freeze).
#   15,000 is the run's own FRL_ACTOR_FREEZE, the warm-up it had at its start.
# WHY: both resumes from 175,000 lost ground in their first 20,000 decisions, with a charge of 50 (466554) and
#   of 10 (466557): temperature 0.088 -> 0.14-0.20, actor-critic steering gap 0.24 -> 0.37-0.42, training goal
#   success 0.65 -> 0.44 and 46-55 m per fault (466557), against 0.082-0.088, 0.23-0.26, 0.66-0.79 and 65-85 m
#   in the run that was never restarted (466519) over the same steps. With charge 10 the reward per decision
#   was unchanged (0.9-1.7 against 0.8-1.8), so the charge is not the cause. A checkpoint does not hold the
#   replay; the resumed actor was being updated from the first 1,000 rows at 8 updates a decision.
# NOT SEPARATED: this run still carries the charge of 10. If it holds the old run's level, the restart was
#   the cause; whether the charge then helps is read from m_per_fault and the validation score afterwards.
# Start with FRL_RESUME=<frl_c0actor_priv_4towns_lc01_miss_2m>/step_175000 under a NEW run name.
. "$REPO/slurm/cluster_frl_c0actor_privcritic_4towns_ar2_lc01_miss_fault10_resume_par.env"
